IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006 (WA) -- the questions of a person under 18 found with, or trying to get,
-- tobacco, a smoking implement or a vape: whether my possession is an offence or only the sale and supply to me (ss 6, 7,
-- 30A, 30B, 106); whether I may buy it and what I must not do to get it (ss 7, 15(2)); proof of age (ss 12, 13, 15(1));
-- and what may be done to me and to what is found on me (ss 98-101).
--
-- SEAT: the minor (a person who has not reached 18 years of age) with a vape or tobacco. Every decision is phrased as that
-- person would ask it: "Is my possession an offence?", "Was the sale to me an offence?", "Is this document proof of my
-- age?", "May my vape be taken, and do I get it back?", "Must I give my name?". Sections addressed to sellers,
-- investigators and police are encoded for what they mean for the minor.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 6, s 7, s 12, s 13, s 15, s 30A(1), (3), s 30B(1)-(6), s 98, s 99, s 100, s 101, s 106; the
-- Glossary definitions of "tobacco product", "tobacco smoking implement", "vaping product", "vaping device", "vaping
-- substance", "vaping accessory", "illicit tobacco product", "prohibited product", "therapeutic vaping product", "sell",
-- "supply", "smoke" and the tier 1 and tier 4 penalties.
--
-- Edition: the compilation "with editorial changes as at 14 May 2026", including the Tobacco Products Control Amendment
-- Act 2026 (No. 1 of 2026; Pt. 2 in force 13 May 2026), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49390.txt
-- (retrieved 7 September 2026). No regulations are deposited: the personal use, commercial and large commercial
-- quantities (s 30B(1)), the "prescribed document" for proof of age (s 15(1)(c)) and the conditions under which a
-- therapeutic vaping product may be sold or held (ss 30A(3), 30B(6)) are INPUTS here.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: licensing (Pts 2 Div 2 and 4) beyond s 18A in a comment; advertising and promotion (Pt 3); display and
-- signage (ss 22-26) except as the s 13(2)(d) fact; smoking-place offences (ss 107A-107D, including smoking in a car with
-- a child under 17); investigations (Pt 6), prosecutions, forfeiture and closure orders; the Act as it stood before
-- 13 May 2026 (not deposited -- see `Does the deposited edition answer for`); the Medicines and Poisons Act 2014 (WA),
-- which governs nicotine as a poison and is outside "tobacco product" (Glossary (b)(i)).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006 (WA)`

§§ `edition`

-- Compilation table: Tobacco Products Control Amendment Act 2026, No. 1 of 2026, "Pt. 2: 13 May 2026". Part 2 inserted
-- Division 3 of Part 2 (ss 30A, 30B: "Inserted: No. 1 of 2026 s. 34") and brought vaping products into the Act. The text
-- in force before that day is not deposited, so a question about an earlier day is answered "not answered".
`the day the deposited edition took effect` MEANS Date 13 5 2026

@export Does the deposited edition of the Act answer for this day (on or after 13 May 2026)?
GIVEN `d` IS A DATE @desc The day of the event
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the deposited edition answer for` `d` IF
    Day `d` AT LEAST Day `the day the deposited edition took effect`

§§ `Glossary -- what the item is`

-- "tobacco product (a) means (i) tobacco in a form prepared for human consumption or use; or (ii) a cigarette or cigar
-- ...; or (iii) a product prepared for smoking that contains a herb or other plant matter ... but (b) does not include
-- (i) nicotine, or a product that contains nicotine, in a form that is a poison as defined in the Medicines and Poisons
-- Act 2014".
-- "illicit tobacco product" -- a tobacco product that contravenes a tobacco product requirement or a tobacco packaging
-- requirement (or a prescribed law or requirement).
-- "tobacco smoking implement (a) means cigarette papers, a cigarette rolling machine, pipe, or other thing designed to be
-- used in the process of smoking a tobacco product ...; but (b) does not include matches or a cigarette lighter".
-- "vaping product" -- a vaping accessory, vaping device, vaping substance, or a product presented as one of them; a vaping
-- device may be one "even if it resembles or functions as a toy, food, drink ..." (Glossary cl. 1(2)).
-- "therapeutic vaping product means a vaping product that is a therapeutic good as defined in the Therapeutic Goods Act
-- 1989 (Cth) section 3(1)".
DECLARE `Kind of item` IS ONE OF
    `a tobacco product (cigarette, cigar, loose tobacco or herbal smoking product) that meets the packaging and product requirements`
    `an illicit tobacco product (one that breaks a tobacco product or packaging requirement)`
    `a vaping product (a vape, pod, cartridge or vaping liquid, with or without nicotine)`
    `a therapeutic vaping product (a vaping product that is a therapeutic good)`
    `a tobacco smoking implement (cigarette papers, rolling machine or pipe)`
    `matches or a cigarette lighter`
    `a food, toy or other product designed to look like a tobacco or vaping product`
    `something else`

GIVEN `k` IS A `Kind of item`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it a tobacco product` IF
    CONSIDER `k`
    WHEN `a tobacco product (cigarette, cigar, loose tobacco or herbal smoking product) that meets the packaging and product requirements` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an illicit tobacco product (one that breaks a tobacco product or packaging requirement)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `k` IS A `Kind of item`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it a vaping product` IF
    CONSIDER `k`
    WHEN `a vaping product (a vape, pod, cartridge or vaping liquid, with or without nicotine)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a therapeutic vaping product (a vaping product that is a therapeutic good)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- "prohibited product means (a) an illicit tobacco product; or (b) a vaping product; or (c) a product prescribed ...".
@export Is what I have a prohibited product under the Act?
GIVEN `k` IS A `Kind of item` @desc What the item is
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it a prohibited product` IF
        `k` EQUALS `an illicit tobacco product (one that breaks a tobacco product or packaging requirement)`
    OR  `Is it a vaping product` `k`

-- s 6 and s 7 reach "a tobacco product or a tobacco smoking implement" only.
GIVEN `k` IS A `Kind of item`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is a tobacco product or a tobacco smoking implement` MEANS
        `Is it a tobacco product` `k`
    OR  `k` EQUALS `a tobacco smoking implement (cigarette papers, rolling machine or pipe)`

§§ `what I hold, and the facts I can state`

-- One item (or one holding of one kind of prohibited product), as the minor could describe it. The three quantities
-- are "prescribed by the regulations" (s 30B(1)); the regulations are not deposited, so they are inputs in the
-- regulations' own unit. Whether a therapeutic vaping product is sold or held on the prescribed conditions (ss 30A(3),
-- 30B(6)) is likewise asked.
DECLARE `My item` HAS
    `what it is`                                         IS A `Kind of item`
    `the day`                                            IS A DATE
    `my age in years`                                    IS A NUMBER
    `how much I hold`                                    IS A NUMBER
    `the personal use quantity for that kind`            IS A NUMBER   -- s 30B(1): prescribed
    `the commercial quantity for that kind`              IS A NUMBER   -- s 30B(1): prescribed
    `the large commercial quantity for that kind`        IS A NUMBER   -- s 30B(1): prescribed
    `the prescribed therapeutic conditions are met`      IS A BOOLEAN  -- ss 30A(3), 30B(6)

§§ `30B -- is my possession an offence`

-- s 30B(2): "A person who possesses a prohibited product commits a crime."
-- s 30B(3): "Subsection (2) does not apply in relation to the possession of a quantity of a prohibited product that is
-- equal to or less than the personal use quantity".
-- s 30B(4): "A person who possesses a quantity ... equal to or greater than the commercial quantity ... commits a crime."
-- s 30B(5): the same for "the large commercial quantity".
-- s 30B(6): "Subsections (2), (4) and (5) do not apply in relation to the possession of a therapeutic vaping product ...
-- if the possession satisfies conditions prescribed by the regulations".
-- No section makes it an offence for anyone, of any age, to possess a tobacco product that is not illicit or a tobacco
-- smoking implement; s 18AA reaches only possession "for the purposes of sale". The minor's age is read by nothing here.
DECLARE `What my possession is` IS ONE OF
    `not answered: the day is before the deposited edition (13 May 2026)`
    `no offence: the Act makes no offence of possessing this`
    `no offence: a therapeutic vaping product held on the prescribed conditions (s 30B(6))`
    `no offence: no more than the personal use quantity (s 30B(3))`
    `an offence under s 30B(2): more than the personal use quantity`
    `an offence under s 30B(4): at least the commercial quantity`
    `an offence under s 30B(5): at least the large commercial quantity`

@export Is my possession of this item an offence under the Act, and which?
GIVEN `i` IS A `My item` @desc The item and the facts about it
GIVETH A `What my possession is`
DECIDE `Is my possession an offence` IS
    IF NOT `Does the deposited edition answer for` (`i`'s `the day`)
    THEN `not answered: the day is before the deposited edition (13 May 2026)`
    ELSE IF NOT `Is it a prohibited product` (`i`'s `what it is`)
         THEN `no offence: the Act makes no offence of possessing this`
         ELSE IF     `i`'s `what it is` EQUALS `a therapeutic vaping product (a vaping product that is a therapeutic good)`
                 AND `i`'s `the prescribed therapeutic conditions are met`
              THEN `no offence: a therapeutic vaping product held on the prescribed conditions (s 30B(6))`
              ELSE IF `i`'s `how much I hold` AT LEAST `i`'s `the large commercial quantity for that kind`
                   THEN `an offence under s 30B(5): at least the large commercial quantity`
                   ELSE IF `i`'s `how much I hold` AT LEAST `i`'s `the commercial quantity for that kind`
                        THEN `an offence under s 30B(4): at least the commercial quantity`
                        ELSE IF `i`'s `how much I hold` AT MOST `i`'s `the personal use quantity for that kind`
                             THEN `no offence: no more than the personal use quantity (s 30B(3))`
                             ELSE `an offence under s 30B(2): more than the personal use quantity`

-- Penalties. s 30B(2): "tier 4 penalty" -- for an individual, first offence, "imprisonment for 10 years and a fine of
-- $600 000" (second or subsequent: $1 200 000); "tier 4 summary penalty" -- first offence "imprisonment for 3 years and
-- a fine of $120 000". s 30B(4)(a): "imprisonment for 15 years and a fine of $2 100 000"; s 30B(5)(a): "imprisonment for
-- 15 years and a fine of $4 200 000". First offence, individual, on indictment.
@export What is the most I can be fined for my possession, in dollars (first offence, on indictment)?
GIVEN `i` IS A `My item` @desc The item and the facts about it
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for my possession` IS
    CONSIDER `Is my possession an offence` `i`
    WHEN `an offence under s 30B(2): more than the personal use quantity` THEN 600000
    WHEN `an offence under s 30B(4): at least the commercial quantity` THEN 2100000
    WHEN `an offence under s 30B(5): at least the large commercial quantity` THEN 4200000
    OTHERWISE 0

§§ `6, 7, 30A, 106 -- was the sale or supply to me an offence`

-- s 6: "A person must not sell, supply or deliver a tobacco product or a tobacco smoking implement to a person who has not
-- reached 18 years of age. Penalty: tier 1 penalty."
-- s 30A(1): "A person who sells or supplies a prohibited product commits a crime." -- to anyone, of any age.
-- s 30A(3): not "the sale or supply of a therapeutic vaping product if the sale or supply satisfies conditions prescribed".
-- Glossary: "supply includes to provide, or offer to provide, whether or not gratuitously" -- so a friend who hands me a
-- vape supplies it.
DECLARE `What the supply to me is` IS ONE OF
    `not answered: the day is before the deposited edition (13 May 2026)`
    `no offence under this Act`
    `an offence under s 6 (to a person under 18)`
    `an offence under s 30A (a prohibited product, to anyone)`
    `an offence under both s 6 and s 30A`

@export Was selling or supplying this item to me an offence under the Act, and which?
GIVEN `i` IS A `My item` @desc The item and the facts about it
GIVETH A `What the supply to me is`
DECIDE `Was the supply to me an offence` IS
    IF NOT `Does the deposited edition answer for` (`i`'s `the day`)
    THEN `not answered: the day is before the deposited edition (13 May 2026)`
    ELSE IF `s 6` AND `s 30A`
         THEN `an offence under both s 6 and s 30A`
         ELSE IF `s 6`
              THEN `an offence under s 6 (to a person under 18)`
              ELSE IF `s 30A`
                   THEN `an offence under s 30A (a prohibited product, to anyone)`
                   ELSE `no offence under this Act`
    WHERE
        `s 6` MEANS     `it is a tobacco product or a tobacco smoking implement` (`i`'s `what it is`)
                    AND `i`'s `my age in years` LESS THAN 18
        `s 30A` MEANS     `Is it a prohibited product` (`i`'s `what it is`)
                      AND (NOT (    `i`'s `what it is` EQUALS `a therapeutic vaping product (a vaping product that is a therapeutic good)`
                                AND `i`'s `the prescribed therapeutic conditions are met`))

-- s 106: "A person must not sell any food, toy or other product that is not a tobacco product or a vaping product but is
-- (a) designed to resemble a tobacco product, a vaping product or a package". Penalty: tier 2. It reaches look-alikes,
-- not real vapes, and does not depend on the buyer's age.
@export Was selling me this item an offence under s 106 (a look-alike of tobacco or a vape)?
GIVEN `k` IS A `Kind of item` @desc What the item is
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was selling me a look-alike an offence` IF
    `k` EQUALS `a food, toy or other product designed to look like a tobacco or vaping product`

-- Glossary "tier 1 penalty": individual, first offence $10 000, second or subsequent $20 000; body corporate $50 000 /
-- $100 000. What the seller who broke s 6 risks.
@export What is the most the seller can be fined for selling tobacco to me under s 6, in dollars?
GIVEN `the seller is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller is a company
      `it is the seller's second or later offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller has offended before
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most the seller can be fined under s 6` IS
    IF `the seller is a body corporate`
    THEN IF `it is the seller's second or later offence` THEN 100000 ELSE 50000
    ELSE IF `it is the seller's second or later offence` THEN 20000 ELSE 10000

§§ `7, 15(2) -- may I buy it, and how not to`

-- No section makes it an offence for the minor to buy or try to buy tobacco. But:
-- s 7: "A person must not purchase a tobacco product or a tobacco smoking implement on behalf of a person who has not
-- reached 18 years of age." -- the adult who buys for me offends (tier 1); for a vape, the adult who hands it on supplies
-- it (s 30A).
-- s 15(2): "A person must not, for the purpose of obtaining a tobacco product or a tobacco smoking implement use (a)
-- another person's document of identification; or (b) a document of identification that has been forged or tampered
-- with. Penalty for this subsection: a fine of $1 000."
@export Would I commit an offence in getting this item (using someone else's or a forged ID, s 15(2))?
GIVEN `k` IS A `Kind of item` @desc What the item is
      `I used another person's ID` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you used someone else's identification
      `I used a forged or tampered ID` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you used a forged or altered identification
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Would I offend in getting it` IF
        `it is a tobacco product or a tobacco smoking implement` `k`
    AND (`I used another person's ID` OR `I used a forged or tampered ID`)

@export Would an adult who buys this item for me commit an offence, and which?
GIVEN `k` IS A `Kind of item` @desc What the item is
      `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Would an adult buying it for me offend` IS
    IF `it is a tobacco product or a tobacco smoking implement` `k` AND `my age in years` LESS THAN 18
    THEN IF `Is it a prohibited product` `k` THEN "s 7 and s 30A" ELSE "s 7"
    ELSE IF `Is it a prohibited product` `k` AND (NOT (`k` EQUALS `a therapeutic vaping product (a vaping product that is a therapeutic good)`))
         THEN "s 30A, by supplying it to me"
         ELSE "no offence under this Act"

§§ `12, 13, 15(1) -- proof of age`

-- s 15(1): "(a) a current passport; (b) a current Australian driver's licence; (c) a prescribed document, that bears a
-- photograph of the person and indicates by reference to the person's date of birth or otherwise that the person has
-- reached 18 years of age."
DECLARE `Kind of document` IS ONE OF
    `a current passport`
    `a current Australian driver's licence`
    `a prescribed document`
    `an expired passport or licence`
    `a student card or other document`

@export Is this document proof that I have reached 18 (s 15(1))?
GIVEN `doc` IS A `Kind of document` @desc The document you show
      `it has my photograph` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it bears your photograph
      `it shows I am 18 or over` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it shows, by date of birth or otherwise, that you have reached 18
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this document proof of my age` IF
        (    `doc` EQUALS `a current passport`
         OR  `doc` EQUALS `a current Australian driver's licence`
         OR  `doc` EQUALS `a prescribed document`)
    AND `it has my photograph`
    AND `it shows I am 18 or over`

-- s 12: a person asked at licensed retail premises to sell, asked to help with a vending machine, or asked to deliver,
-- "may refuse to do so unless the person who is to take possession ... produces evidence that he or she has reached 18
-- years of age". It reaches tobacco products and implements; a vape may not be sold to me at all (s 30A).
@export May the seller refuse to sell me this item unless I prove I am 18 (s 12)?
GIVEN `k` IS A `Kind of item` @desc What the item is
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the seller refuse me without proof of age` IF
    `it is a tobacco product or a tobacco smoking implement` `k`

-- s 13(2): a defence to s 6, 7, 8(1) and 9 "to prove (a) that ... the person charged had no reason to believe that the
-- receiver had not reached 18 years of age; and (b) that ... the receiver had reached 14 years of age; and (c) that at or
-- before the relevant time the receiver had produced evidence that the receiver had reached 18 years of age; and (d) that
-- ... there was compliance with section 25(1) or (2)" (the warning signs). Whether the seller had reason to believe is
-- the court's judgment on the seller's state of mind, asked as a fact.
@export Does the seller who sold me tobacco have the s 13 defence?
GIVEN `the seller had no reason to believe I was under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As the court would find it
      `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age at the time
      `I produced evidence that I was 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you showed a s 15(1) document saying you were 18
      `the s 25 warning signs were displayed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the required warning signs were up
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the seller have the s 13 defence` IF
        `the seller had no reason to believe I was under 18`
    AND `my age in years` AT LEAST 14
    AND `I produced evidence that I was 18`
    AND `the s 25 warning signs were displayed`

§§ `98-101 -- what may be done to me and to what is found on me`

-- s 98: "young person means a person who an investigator suspects on reasonable grounds has not reached 18 years of age".
-- s 99(1), (2): an investigator, or a police officer ("and use reasonable force to do so"), "may seize any tobacco
-- product, tobacco smoking implement or prohibited product from a young person".
-- s 99(3): not "unless (a) the person has been requested to produce a document mentioned in section 15(1) showing that the
-- person has reached 18 years of age; and (b) the document was not produced at the time of the request".
-- The officer's reasonable suspicion is the officer's judgment, asked as a fact. s 79(1): "a police officer (a)
-- may exercise the powers, and perform the functions, of an investigator" -- so the ss 100 and 101 powers are a police
-- officer's too.
DECLARE `Who found me` IS ONE OF
    `an investigator`
    `a police officer`
    `someone else`

@export May the item be taken from me (s 99)?
GIVEN `k` IS A `Kind of item` @desc What the item is
      `who` IS A `Who found me` @desc Who found you with it
      `they suspect on reasonable grounds I am under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As the officer would say
      `I was asked for a s 15(1) document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were asked for a passport, licence or prescribed document
      `I produced one showing I am 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you showed such a document then and there
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the item be taken from me` IF
        (`it is a tobacco product or a tobacco smoking implement` `k` OR `Is it a prohibited product` `k`)
    AND (NOT (`who` EQUALS `someone else`))
    AND `they suspect on reasonable grounds I am under 18`
    AND `I was asked for a s 15(1) document`
    AND (NOT `I produced one showing I am 18`)

@export May force be used to take the item from me (s 99(2))?
GIVEN `who` IS A `Who found me` @desc Who found you with it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May force be used to take it` IF
    `who` EQUALS `a police officer`

-- s 99(4): "A tobacco smoking implement, or a tobacco product that is not a prohibited product, that is seized ... (a) is
-- to be returned ... if, within 7 days of the seizure, the person produces to the investigator a document mentioned in
-- section 15(1) showing that the person had reached 18 years of age at the time of the seizure; or (b) if not returned
-- ..., is to be destroyed in an approved manner."
-- s 99(5): "A prohibited product that is seized ... is to be destroyed in an approved manner."
DECLARE `What happens to my seized item` IS ONE OF
    `returned to me`
    `destroyed`

@export What happens to my item after it is taken (s 99(4), (5))?
GIVEN `k` IS A `Kind of item` @desc What the item is
      `days after seizure I produced proof I was 18` IS A NUMBER @desc Days after the seizure you showed a s 15(1) document; a large number if never
      `the proof shows I was 18 when it was taken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that document shows you had reached 18 at the seizure
GIVETH A `What happens to my seized item`
DECIDE `What happens to my seized item` IS
    IF `Is it a prohibited product` `k`
    THEN `destroyed`
    ELSE IF     `days after seizure I produced proof I was 18` AT MOST 7
            AND `the proof shows I was 18 when it was taken`
         THEN `returned to me`
         ELSE `destroyed`

-- s 100(1): an investigator who finds a young person "smoking or in possession of a tobacco product, prohibited product
-- or tobacco smoking implement" may require (a) my name and address, (b) a parent's name and address, (c) "information
-- relating to the identity of any person who supplied" it.
-- s 100(2): "A person who has reached 14 years of age (a) must comply ...; and (b) must not provide false or misleading
-- information ... Penalty for this subsection: a fine of $1 000."
-- "smoke" includes holding "a vaping device that is generating or releasing ... aerosol or vapour".
@export Must I give my name and address, my parent's, and who supplied me, when asked (s 100)?
GIVEN `who` IS A `Who found me` @desc Who found you
      `I was smoking or vaping or had the item` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were found smoking, vaping or in possession
      `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give my details` IF
        (NOT (`who` EQUALS `someone else`))
    AND `I was smoking or vaping or had the item`
    AND `my age in years` AT LEAST 14

@export What is the most I can be fined for refusing or lying under s 100, in dollars?
GIVEN `who` IS A `Who found me` @desc Who found you
      `I was smoking or vaping or had the item` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were found smoking, vaping or in possession
      `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined under s 100` IS
    IF `Must I give my details` `who` `I was smoking or vaping or had the item` `my age in years`
    THEN 1000
    ELSE 0

-- s 101: the investigator "may (a) notify a parent of the young person of the finding; (b) provide the young person or a
-- parent ... with an approved guide" -- also where I was "obtaining or attempting to obtain" it.
@export May my parent be told (s 101)?
GIVEN `who` IS A `Who found me` @desc Who found you
      `I was smoking, vaping, had the item or was trying to get it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc What you were found doing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my parent be told` IF
        (NOT (`who` EQUALS `someone else`))
    AND `I was smoking, vaping, had the item or was trying to get it`
